@CL 192[2]. Stripped of the exuviae which were composed of the elements in waters and earths...

@ISB 9[3]. The nature of the sun's heat is similar to the heat from elementary fire.

@10. Regarded in itself, elementary fire is relatively dead.

@TCR 20[end]. As of a conflux of elements into such a form...

@103[2]. Within a certain envelope of elements from nature...

@125[2]. The sun... must act by means of the element in which the subject is.

@491[2]. The earth merely supplies fluids and elements, and the shrubs appropriate them...

@504[6]. Korean the elements rise up through the root, unless...

