@911[2]. Therefore, when spiritual light inflows into natural light with the man who is reading the Word, he is enlightened, and sees the truths therein; for truths are the objects of spiritual light. The Word in the sense of the letter is of such a character, that the more a man is enlightened by means of the influx of the light of Heaven, the more he sees truths from their connection and thus from their form.

@919. "Because the glory of God enlightened it" (Revelation 21:19) = that the men of that Church... will be in spiritual light from the Divine truth of the Word from the Lord alone.

@920. To "walk in the light of the New Jerusalem" = to perceive and see Divine truths from interior enlightenment, and to live according to them.

